      "problem": "What picture is missing from the division model below?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14129811/assets/9cc5d672cb3c12ceb7704f5136e9b7ecae61d11a9418acf3b8e1cbb9e8f044f7.png)",
      "worked_solution": "Notice that in the model, we have $\\dfrac{1}{3}$ on the left.\n\nSince we need to divide by $\\color{blue}3$, we split the whole into $\\color{blue}3$ equal parts horizontally.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14129811/assets/30f9bbc604d35a9a15e1418c0cf80eca87fe4d704287c15fb8de7426eb9e3de9.png)\n\nFrom the picture on the right, we obtain that the shaded part represents $\\dfrac{1}{9}$ of the whole.\n\nSo, the missing picture is:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14129811/assets/951a4bc0607c53aa0c5ed9cebe664b630acf226a6f9844fd9d1b8e6ae952d0ed.png)",
